Issues.Body:
ngtsc's `ImportManager` rebuilds every file it adds imports to as `[...existing import statements, ...generated imports, ...rest of the file]`, and [`isImportStatement`](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/73911c8/packages/compiler-cli/src/ngtsc/translator/src/import_manager/import_typescript_transform.ts#L144-L148) counts `import X = …` (including `export import X = …`) as an import statement. So `ngtsc` moves every `import X = …` to the top of the file, together with any `import` declarations written further down. `ngp` only hoisted `import` declarations and left `import X = …` where it was written. When code earlier in the file reads the alias while the module loads, `ngtsc`'s output works and `ngp`'s throws. This shows up in Google3, e.g. `export import LabelStyleEnum = formTypes.LabelStyleEnum;` at line 305 of a file that `ngtsc` compiles with the assignment right after the imports.

This change:
1. Collects the top-level `import X = …` statements in `ng-analyze` and sends them to the emitter with their spans.
2. Hoists them together with the late `import` declarations, in source order, as `ngtsc` does.
3. Only hoists in a file that gets generated imports, i.e. one with a compiled class. `ngtsc` leaves a file whose classes are all `jit: true` untouched, but `ngp` still adds an `@angular/core` import there, so it no longer hoists late `import` declarations in such a file either.

This changes runtime behavior in both directions, each time to match `ngtsc`. Code that reads an `import X = …` alias before the line it's written on now loads instead of throwing. Code with an `import X = Local.Y` written after a local `namespace` or `enum` named `Local` now breaks, as it does with `ngtsc`: the alias moves above the declaration and reads `undefined.Y` at runtime (for an `enum`, the type-checked output also reports TS2450). Valid Google3 code can't hit this, because it already crashes under `ngtsc`. The existing `imports_equals_and_non_angular_hoisting` golden records this, and there's a `TODO` at the hoisting site.

### Input

```ts
// ns.ts
export namespace formTypes {
  export enum LabelStyleEnum {
    A = 'a',
    B = 'b',
  }
}

// app.ts
import {Component, InjectionToken} from '@angular/core';
import {formTypes} from './ns';

export const LABEL_STYLE = new InjectionToken<string>('LABEL_STYLE');

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  template: '',
  providers: [{provide: LABEL_STYLE, useValue: LabelStyleEnum.B}],
})
export class AppComponent {}

export import LabelStyleEnum = formTypes.LabelStyleEnum;
```

### Output Before Fix (`ngp`)

```ts
import {Component, InjectionToken} from '@angular/core';
import {formTypes} from './ns';
// @ts-ignore
import * as i0 from '@angular/core';

export const LABEL_STYLE = new InjectionToken<string>('LABEL_STYLE');

export class AppComponent {
  // ...
  static ɵcmp = /*@__PURE__*/ i0.ɵɵdefineComponent({
    // ...
    features: [i0.ɵɵProvidersFeature([{provide: LABEL_STYLE, useValue: LabelStyleEnum.B}])],
  });
}

export import LabelStyleEnum = formTypes.LabelStyleEnum;
```

Loading the module throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'B')`.

### Output After Fix (`ngp` — matches `ngtsc`)

```ts
import {Component, InjectionToken} from '@angular/core';
import {formTypes} from './ns';
export import LabelStyleEnum = formTypes.LabelStyleEnum;
// @ts-ignore
import * as i0 from '@angular/core';

export const LABEL_STYLE = new InjectionToken<string>('LABEL_STYLE');

export class AppComponent {
  // ...
  static ɵcmp = /*@__PURE__*/ i0.ɵɵdefineComponent({
    // ...
    features: [i0.ɵɵProvidersFeature([{provide: LABEL_STYLE, useValue: LabelStyleEnum.B}])],
  });
}
```

The module loads, as `ngtsc`'s output does.

In local and `emitDeclarationOnly` compilation, `ngtsc`'s `extractHostDirectives` keeps every `hostDirectives` entry or reports it. An entry that evaluates to a reference is emitted as one. An entry that is still dynamic is emitted verbatim (`WrappedNodeExpr`) when it's written as an identifier or property access, and any other expression reports `NG11003`. Without `emitDeclarationOnly`, the partial evaluator still resolves values across the compilation unit.

`ng-analyze` dropped entries silently instead. An undeclared identifier, a property access on one, or a string disappeared from the emitted metadata. An entry that depended on another file (an imported array, a spread of one, a conditional on an imported flag, or an imported `inputs` mapping) dropped the whole `hostDirectives` field.

This change:
1. Evaluates `hostDirectives` across the compilation unit without `emitDeclarationOnly`. Under `emitDeclarationOnly`, only ambient `.d.ts` globals fold (e.g. `COMPILED ? DirA : DirB`).
2. Emits a still-dynamic entry verbatim when its array element is an identifier or property access, and reports `NG11003` otherwise. An entry flagged as an unsupported expression stays flagged unless it folds to a concrete value, because `ngtsc` re-anchors a dynamic value on the outermost expression it evaluated.
3. Reports `NG1010` for a non-array value or a non-reference entry. An `inputs`/`outputs` value that isn't an array yields no mapping instead of dropping the entry, matching `parseHostDirectivesMapping`.

### Input

```ts
// deps.ts
import {Directive} from '@angular/core';

@Directive({selector: '[depA]'})
export class DepA {}

@Directive({selector: '[depB]'})
export class DepB {}

export const HOST_DIRECTIVES = [DepA, DepB];

// app.ts (compiled with compilationMode: 'experimental-local')
import {Component} from '@angular/core';
import {HOST_DIRECTIVES} from './deps';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  template: '',
  hostDirectives: HOST_DIRECTIVES,
})
export class AppComponent {}
```

### Output Before Fix (`ngp`)

```ts
static ɵcmp = /*@__PURE__*/ i0.ɵɵdefineComponent({
  type: AppComponent,
  selectors: [['app-root']],
  decls: 0,
  vars: 0,
  template: function AppComponent_Template(rf: number, ctx: any): any {},
  encapsulation: 2,
});
```

### Output After Fix (`ngp` — matches `ngtsc`)

```ts
static ɵcmp = /*@__PURE__*/ i0.ɵɵdefineComponent({
  type: AppComponent,
  selectors: [['app-root']],
  features: [i0.ɵɵHostDirectivesFeature([i1.DepA, i1.DepB])],
  decls: 0,
  vars: 0,
  template: function AppComponent_Template(rf: number, ctx: any): any {},
  encapsulation: 2,
});
```
